{"parentUuid":"5e00920a-a531-4228-ad30-f9ecf03f09c8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a3d28b89aecf59fd1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019g6CK6Xe49HjuVEbc4CJiJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## ARCH Engine architecture, governance & agent organization\n2\t  # ARCH.REQ Requirements & configuration profiles\n3\t     ARCH.REQ.game-requirements | Capture target game requirements (genre, scale, platforms, online model) as engine requirements | engine-architect E \n4\t     ARCH.REQ.profiles | Engine configuration profiles & feature sets (indie 2D → AAA open-world online) | engine-architect E \n5\t     ARCH.REQ.hardware-tiers | Target hardware tier definitions (portable, mobile, console, PC min/rec/high) | engine-architect E ['performance-architect']\n6\t     ARCH.REQ.non-goals | Capability & non-goal register (what the engine deliberately does not do) | engine-architect E \n7\t  # ARCH.STRUCT Structure & boundaries\n8\t     ARCH.STRUCT.layering | Layering rules & module boundaries | engine-architect E \n9\t     ARCH.STRUCT.contracts | Contract registry between subsystems | engine-architect E \n10\t     ARCH.STRUCT.build-buy | Build / integrate / buy decisions (middleware, OSS) | engine-architect E ['architecture-governance']\n11\t     ARCH.STRUCT.replaceability | Subsystem replaceability & optionality (modules absent in small profiles) | engine-architect E \n12\t     ARCH.STRUCT.conventions | Global conventions: units, handedness, up-axis, coordinate spaces | engine-architect E ['math-simd-numerics']\n13\t     ARCH.STRUCT.arbitration | Cross-domain arbitration & escalation of boundary disputes | engine-architect E \n14\t  # ARCH.GOV Architecture governance\n15\t     ARCH.GOV.adr | ADR lifecycle with evidence, alternatives, revisit conditions | architecture-governance E \n16\t     ARCH.GOV.fitness | Automated architectural fitness functions (layering, dependency, contract conformance) | architecture-governance E \n17\t     ARCH.GOV.anti-legacy | Anti-legacy review of designs against flagged patterns | architecture-governance E \n18\t     ARCH.GOV.radar | Technology radar & maturity tiers with promotion criteria | architecture-governance E ['research-evidence']\n19\t     ARCH.GOV.coding-standard | Coding standard & language subset | architecture-governance E ['core-runtime-architect']\n20\t  # ARCH.EVID Research & evidence\n21\t     ARCH.EVID.grading | Source grading & provenance tiers | research-evidence E \n22\t     ARCH.EVID.survey | Literature survey protocol per decision | research-evidence E \n23\t     ARCH.EVID.spike | Prototype/spike protocol producing evidence where literature is thin | research-evidence E \n24\t     ARCH.EVID.claims | Benchmark-backed claims standard | research-evidence E ['perf-benchmarking']\n25\t  # ARCH.ORG Agent organization\n26\t     ARCH.ORG.decomposition | Milestone → task decomposition by skill territory | program-orchestration E \n27\t     ARCH.ORG.ownership-ledger | Ownership ledger & territory locks | program-orchestration E \n28\t     ARCH.ORG.integration | Integration sequencing & milestone vertical slices | program-orchestration E \n29\t     ARCH.ORG.change-requests | Contract change-request protocol between agents | program-orchestration E ['architecture-governance']\n30\t     ARCH.ORG.critic-gates | Scheduling critic gates per stage | program-orchestration E \n31\t## PLAT Platform & hardware abstraction\n32\t  # PLAT.PAL Platform abstraction layer\n33\t     PLAT.PAL.os | OS services abstraction (threads, virtual memory, files, time, dynamic libraries) | platform-architect E \n34\t     PLAT.PAL.cpu-topology | CPU topology & feature discovery (hybrid cores, SMT, caches, NUMA, ISA) | platform-architect E ['job-system-task-graph']\n35\t     PLAT.PAL.windowing | Windowing & surfaces | platform-architect E \n36\t     PLAT.PAL.lifecycle | Process lifecycle (suspend, resume, constrained, terminate) | platform-architect E ['platform-console', 'platform-mobile-portable']\n37\t     PLAT.PAL.capability-tiers | Platform capability tiers & feature query | platform-architect E \n38\t     PLAT.PAL.web | Web target (WASM + WebGPU) | platform-architect M \n39\t     PLAT.PAL.cloud-streaming | Cloud-streaming targets (latency, encode, input) | platform-architect M \n40\t  # PLAT.DESK Desktop & handheld PC\n41\t     PLAT.DESK.os-integration | Windows / Linux / SteamOS / macOS integration | platform-desktop E \n42\t     PLAT.DESK.display | Display enumeration, modes, DPI, HDR & VRR capability | platform-desktop E \n43\t     PLAT.DESK.handheld | Handheld PC specifics (power, resolution, controls) | platform-desktop E \n44\t     PLAT.DESK.server-host | Server host OS specifics (Linux containers) | platform-desktop E ['dedicated-server']\n45\t  # PLAT.CON Console-class platforms\n46\t     PLAT.CON.os-memory | Console OS & memory model (UMA, reserved memory, fixed hardware) | platform-console E \n47\t     PLAT.CON.user-model | Console multi-user model & user/device pairing | platform-console E \n48\t     PLAT.CON.suspend | Suspend / resume / quick-resume | platform-console E \n49\t     PLAT.CON.devkit | Devkit workflows & SDK toolchains | platform-console E ['build-system-toolchains']\n50\t  # PLAT.MOB Mobile & portable\n51\t     PLAT.MOB.os | iOS / Android / portable-console integration | platform-mobile-portable E \n52\t     PLAT.MOB.tbdr | Tile-based GPU implications (bandwidth, on-chip memory) | platform-mobile-portable E ['render-graph-scheduling']\n53\t     PLAT.MOB.thermal | Thermal & power adaptivity | platform-mobile-portable E ['performance-architect']\n54\t     PLAT.MOB.storage | Storage & download-size constraints | platform-mobile-portable E \n55\t  # PLAT.SVC Platform & online services integration\n56\t     PLAT.SVC.identity | User identity, sign-in, account linking, crossplay identity | platform-online-services E \n57\t     PLAT.SVC.achievements | Achievements, trophies, activities, rich presence | platform-online-services E \n58\t     PLAT.SVC.entitlements | Entitlements, store, DLC ownership | platform-online-services E \n59\t     PLAT.SVC.cloud-save | Cloud save services | platform-online-services E ['persistence-save']\n60\t     PLAT.SVC.matchmaking | Matchmaking / lobby / session integration boundary | platform-online-services E ['network-architect']\n61\t     PLAT.SVC.remote-config | Remote configuration & feature flags | platform-online-services E \n62\t     PLAT.SVC.moderation | UGC & text-chat moderation service boundary | platform-online-services E ['modding-ugc']\n63\t     PLAT.SVC.capture | Media capture & share integration | platform-online-services E \n64\t  # PLAT.XR XR\n65\t     PLAT.XR.openxr | OpenXR runtime integration | xr-runtime E \n66\t     PLAT.XR.stereo | Stereo / multiview rendering integration | xr-runtime E ['render-architect']\n67\t     PLAT.XR.foveation | Fixed & eye-tracked foveated rendering | xr-runtime M \n68\t     PLAT.XR.reprojection | Reprojection & motion-to-photon latency | xr-runtime E \n69\t     PLAT.XR.input | XR input & hand tracking | xr-runtime E ['input-devices-haptics']\n70\t     PLAT.XR.comfort | Comfort & safety requirements | xr-runtime E \n71\t## CORE Core runtime foundations\n72\t  # CORE.LIFE Lifecycle, modules, configuration, errors\n73\t     CORE.LIFE.boot | Parallel boot via init dependency graph | core-runtime-architect E \n74\t     CORE.LIFE.modules | Module system (static/dynamic linking, init order) | core-runtime-architect E \n75\t     CORE.LIFE.shutdown | Deterministic shutdown & teardown ordering | core-runtime-architect E \n76\t     CORE.LIFE.services | Service registry & dependency-injection policy (no hidden globals) | core-runtime-architect E \n77\t     CORE.LIFE.config | Layered configuration, cvars, command line, per-platform/per-device values | core-runtime-architect E \n78\t     CORE.LIFE.errors | Error-handling & failure model (expected-style results, fatal vs recoverable) | core-runtime-architect E \n79\t     CORE.LIFE.asserts | Assertion tiers & contract checks | core-runtime-architect E ['crash-diagnostics']\n80\t     CORE.LIFE.language | Language standard & compiler feature policy (C++20/23, exceptions/RTTI policy) | core-runtime-architect E \n81\t  # CORE.MATH Math & numerics\n82\t     CORE.MATH.linear | SIMD linear algebra (vectors, matrices, quaternions) | math-simd-numerics E \n83\t     CORE.MATH.geometry | Geometry primitives & intersection tests | math-simd-numerics E \n84\t     CORE.MATH.compgeo | Computational geometry (hulls, triangulation, booleans) | math-simd-numerics E \n85\t     CORE.MATH.robustness | Numerical robustness & precision analysis | math-simd-numerics E \n86\t     CORE.MATH.precision | Double & mixed-precision math for large worlds | math-simd-numerics E ['spatial-transforms']\n87\t     CORE.MATH.deterministic | Cross-platform reproducible math library | math-simd-numerics E ['determinism-replay']\n88\t     CORE.MATH.random | Random numbers & noise functions | math-simd-numerics E \n89\t     CORE.MATH.curves | Curves, splines & interpolation | math-simd-numerics E \n90\t     CORE.MATH.spmd | Wide-SIMD / SPMD kernels & runtime ISA dispatch | math-simd-numerics E ['cpu-performance']\n91\t     CORE.MATH.formats | Half, packed & quantized numeric formats | math-simd-numerics E \n92\t  # CORE.MEM Memory\n93\t     CORE.MEM.virtual | Virtual memory reservation & mapping | memory-allocators E \n94\t     CORE.MEM.allocators | Allocator families (linear/frame, pool, TLSF, slab, buddy) | memory-allocators E \n95\t     CORE.MEM.thread-caches | Thread-local caches & NUMA-aware allocation | memory-allocators E \n96\t     CORE.MEM.tracking | Memory tagging, tracking & attribution | memory-allocators E ['observability-telemetry']\n97\t     CORE.MEM.budget-enforcement | Budget enforcement mechanisms per subsystem | memory-allocators E ['performance-architect']\n98\t     CORE.MEM.fragmentation | Fragmentation control & defragmentation/relocation | memory-allocators E \n99\t     CORE.MEM.debugging | Memory debugging (guard pages, poisoning, sanitizer integration) | memory-allocators E ['robustness-fuzzing']\n100\t     CORE.MEM.oom | Out-of-memory policy & graceful degradation | memory-allocators E \n101\t     CORE.MEM.uma | Unified-memory CPU/GPU accounting | memory-allocators E ['gpu-memory-resources']\n102\t  # CORE.TYPES Core types & containers\n103\t     CORE.TYPES.containers | Containers (arrays, open-addressing hash maps, inline, SoA, intrusive, rings) | containers-core-types E \n104\t     CORE.TYPES.strings | Strings, UTF-8 handling, interned names | containers-core-types E \n105\t     CORE.TYPES.hashing | Non-cryptographic & stable content hashing | containers-core-types E \n106\t     CORE.TYPES.bits | Bit manipulation & bitsets | containers-core-types E \n107\t     CORE.TYPES.algorithms | Sort, search & generic algorithms | containers-core-types E \n108\t     CORE.TYPES.ownership | Span/view & explicit-ownership types | containers-core-types E ['core-runtime-architect']\n109\t  # CORE.CONC Concurrency primitives\n110\t     CORE.CONC.atomics | Memory model & atomics | concurrency-primitives E \n111\t     CORE.CONC.sync | Synchronization primitives (futex-backed locks, events, spin with backoff) | concurrency-primitives E \n112\t     CORE.CONC.lockfree | Lock-free / wait-free structures (MPMC queues, work-stealing deques) | concurrency-primitives E \n113\t     CORE.CONC.reclamation | Safe memory reclamation (epochs, hazard pointers) | concurrency-primitives E \n114\t     CORE.CONC.correctness | Thread-safety annotations & model checking | concurrency-primitives E ['robustness-fuzzing']\n115\t  # CORE.JOBS Jobs, task graphs, fibers\n116\t     CORE.JOBS.scheduler | Work-stealing job scheduler | job-system-task-graph E \n117\t     CORE.JOBS.graph | Task graphs with explicit dependencies | job-system-task-graph E \n118\t     CORE.JOBS.fibers | Fibers and C++20 coroutin