{"parentUuid":"7d083b25-53af-49f8-9ed0-f2d9605dbb46","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a3d28b89aecf59fd1","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfXzNL5BZLTh6S4qCp3w1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016cPtyeMduDQDptaxGdUNWY","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-skills/64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82/scratchpad/skills.txt"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":995,"cache_read_input_tokens":110393,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":995,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016cPtyeMduDQDptaxGdUNWY":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-skills/64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82/scratchpad/skills.txt"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfXzNKmKfDeqC9hEeBK2Z","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"da6d22fa-95f5-4d97-88dc-17a927c6200f","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:45:34.329Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
{"parentUuid":"da6d22fa-95f5-4d97-88dc-17a927c6200f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a3d28b89aecf59fd1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016cPtyeMduDQDptaxGdUNWY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t== engine-architect : Owns the engine's overall architecture: requirements and configuration profiles, layering and module boundaries, the contract registry, global conventions, build/integrate/buy decisions and cross-domain arbitration. Final authority on the boundaries between skills.\n2\t   - Running the ADR, fitness-function and anti-legacy process -> architecture-governance\n3\t   - Scheduling work across agents and the ownership ledger -> program-orchestration\n4\t   - Architecture inside a domain (e.g. shading-path choice) -> render-architect\n5\t== architecture-governance : Runs architecture as an evidence-backed, governed process: ADR lifecycle with revisit conditions, technology radar with maturity tiers and promotion criteria, automated fitness functions (layering, dependency direction, contract conformance), anti-legacy review, coding standard.\n6\t   - Making the architecture decisions themselves -> engine-architect\n7\t   - Grading sources and running spikes -> research-evidence\n8\t   - Test definition of done -> test-architect\n9\t== program-orchestration : Turns architecture into coordinated multi-agent work: decomposes milestones into tasks by skill territory, keeps the ownership ledger and territory locks, sequences integration through vertical slices, routes contract change requests, and schedules critic gates.\n10\t   - Deciding architecture -> engine-architect\n11\t   - CI mechanics -> ci-cd-automation\n12\t   - Release versioning -> build-release-architect\n13\t== research-evidence : Research discipline for every major decision: finds and grades authoritative evidence (production talks, platform docs, peer-reviewed work, reproducible benchmarks), classifies techniques as established / emerging / experimental / speculative, and runs spikes where literature is thin.\n14\t   - Making the decision (the owning skill does, via an ADR) -> architecture-governance\n15\t   - Benchmark infrastructure -> perf-benchmarking\n16\t== performance-architect : Owns performance as a discipline: the hypothesis → instrumentation → measurement → optimization → regression-test loop, budgets per subsystem and hardware tier, the scalability / device-profile framework, and performance gates.\n17\t   - Optimizing a subsystem's code (its owner does, with review) -> cpu-performance\n18\t   - Instrumentation API -> observability-telemetry\n19\t   - Benchmark harness -> perf-benchmarking\n20\t== perf-benchmarking : Benchmark harnesses (micro and representative-workload scenes), automated capture, statistical analysis (variance, significance), regression detection and bisection, dashboards.\n21\t   - Setting budgets -> performance-architect\n22\t   - CI infrastructure -> ci-cd-automation\n23\t== cpu-performance : CPU microarchitecture-level optimization and review: cache and memory-access patterns, vectorization audits, contention and false sharing, hybrid-core and power-aware tuning, PGO/LTO.\n24\t   - Owning subsystem code -> engine-architect\n25\t   - Math library -> math-simd-numerics\n26\t   - Scheduler design -> job-system-task-graph\n27\t== gpu-performance : GPU performance analysis and review: occupancy, bandwidth, cache behavior, barrier and async-compute overlap, vendor tools across PC, console and mobile, GPU power.\n28\t   - Render graph scheduling design -> render-graph-scheduling\n29\t   - Shader authoring for features -> render-architect\n30\t== loading-streaming-performance : End-to-end load time, startup time and hitch elimination (PSO compilation, streaming stalls, GC pauses, synchronous waits), IO throughput analysis.\n31\t   - IO backend implementation -> async-io-storage\n32\t   - PSO cache implementation -> rhi-core\n33\t   - Streaming policy -> resource-streaming-architect\n34\t== test-architect : Test strategy and architecture: per-subsystem test pyramid, frameworks, the test definition of done every skill must meet, contract tests, test content, coverage and mutation policy, flakiness policy.\n35\t   - Running pipelines -> ci-cd-automation\n36\t   - Performance regression -> perf-benchmarking\n37\t   - Rendering image validation -> render-validation\n38\t== render-validation : Rendering correctness validation: golden-image tests with perceptual metrics, tolerances per GPU/driver, comparisons against the reference path tracer, graphics API validation in CI.\n39\t   - Fixing rendering features -> render-architect\n40\t   - Material furnace tests (defines them; this skill runs them) -> material-system\n41\t== functional-automation-soak : Game-level automation: scripted and bot playthroughs, smoke/boot tests, soak and stability runs (memory growth, leaks), hardware/OS compatibility matrix, network harnesses and server load tests.\n42\t   - Unit test frameworks -> test-architect\n43\t   - Device-farm infrastructure -> ci-cd-automation\n44\t== robustness-fuzzing : Robustness engineering: fuzzing every untrusted-input parser (assets, packets, saves, scripts, mods), sanitizer build policy, fault injection (IO errors, OOM, device lost), concurrency stress and schedule perturbation.\n45\t   - Threat model -> security-engineering\n46\t   - Fixing parsers -> serialization-schema\n47\t== certification-compliance : Tracks and pre-validates external requirements: platform certification (TRC/XR/Lotcheck class), age ratings, privacy law, accessibility law (CVAA, EAA), third-party licenses and SBOM, photosensitivity testing.\n48\t   - Implementing platform features -> platform-architect\n49\t   - Implementing accessibility features -> accessibility\n50\t== security-engineering : Threat modeling and trust boundaries for every untrusted input, secure-coding and memory-safety policy, supply-chain security, secrets, anti-tamper boundary, privacy engineering, mod/UGC sandbox policy.\n51\t   - Cheat detection -> anti-cheat-integrity\n52\t   - Fuzzing campaigns -> robustness-fuzzing\n53\t   - Transport encryption implementation -> network-transport\n54\t== anti-cheat-integrity : Cheat resistance for online games: server-authoritative validation patterns (movement, hits, economy), rate limiting, anomaly signals, integration boundary for client anti-cheat middleware.\n55\t   - Replication design -> replication\n56\t   - Transport encryption -> network-transport\n57\t== observability-telemetry : Instrumentation substrate: structured logging, trace zones (CPU, GPU, IO, memory), counters and metrics, profiler integrations, in-game stats, development and live telemetry with privacy consent; zero cost when compiled out.\n58\t   - Crash capture -> crash-diagnostics\n59\t   - Debug drawing and consoles -> visual-debugging-tools\n60\t   - Perf budgets -> performance-architect\n61\t== crash-diagnostics : Crash, hang and GPU-fault capture and reporting: minidumps, symbolication, bucketing and triage, GPU crash dumps, watchdogs, OOM reports, assert reporting.\n62\t   - Emitting GPU breadcrumbs -> rhi-core\n63\t   - Symbol server infrastructure -> ci-cd-automation\n64\t== determinism-replay : Defines determinism levels (none, same-binary, cross-platform) per subsystem and the floating-point and parallel-execution rules that achieve them; owns input/state record-replay and desync detection.\n65\t   - Rollback netcode -> prediction-rollback\n66\t   - Deterministic math implementation -> math-simd-numerics\n67\t== hot-reload-iteration : Owns the reload protocol (change detection, dependency invalidation, state preservation) that assets, shaders, scripts, config and C++ live coding plug into; measures edit → see latency.\n68\t   - Each system's own reload implementation -> resource-streaming-architect\n69\t   - Build system -> build-system-toolchains\n70\t== accessibility : Maps XAG/GAG and legal requirements to engine features and owns subtitles and captions, screen-reader/TTS/STT hooks, colorblind and contrast modes, text scaling, motion and photosensitivity options, assist hooks, and their validation.\n71\t   - Input remapping implementation -> input-system\n72\t   - UI layout engine -> ui-architect\n73\t   - Legal compliance sign-off -> certification-compliance\n74\t== api-lifecycle-migration : Public API surface, semantic versioning and deprecation, ABI policy, engine-upgrade tooling (codemods, data upgraders) and LTS policy, so projects can move across engine versions.\n75\t   - Data schema mechanisms -> serialization-schema\n76\t   - Plugin loading -> plugin-system\n77\t== plugin-system : Plugin architecture: manifests, discovery, dependency resolution, load phases, binary vs source plugins, isolation, distribution format.\n78\t   - Mods & UGC -> modding-ugc\n79\t   - Module linking internals -> core-runtime-architect\n80\t== modding-ugc : Mod and UGC support: mod SDK, content overrides via VFS layering, sandboxed mod scripting, UGC upload and moderation boundaries, mod compatibility across patches.\n81\t   - Sandbox policy -> security-engineering\n82\t   - Script VM -> scripting-runtime\n83\t== developer-experience-docs : Documentation and developer experience: API reference, architecture docs, the sample-project ladder (2D → open-world online) that doubles as integration tests, templates, onboarding, doc testing, error-message standards, DX metrics.\n84\t   - ADR records -> architecture-governance\n85\t   - Iteration-time tooling -> hot-reload-iteration\n86\t== ml-inference-runtime : Runtime neural-network inference shared by neural rendering, animation, audio and AI: GPU (cooperative-vector / tensor) and CPU backends, model packaging and quantization, scheduling within frame budgets, determinism characteristics.\n87\t   - Vendor upscalers -> reconstruction-upscaling\n88\t   - Neural feature design (texture, material, animation) -> texture-streaming-vt\n89\t== core-runtime-architect : Core runtime architecture: layering within core, module system and engine lifecycle (parallel boot, init graph, shutdown), configuration and cvars, error-handling and failure model, language and compiler feature policy.\n90\t   - Allocator design -> memory-allocators\n91\t   - Scheduler -> job-system-task-graph\n92\t   - Frame loop -> frame-orchestration\n93\t== math-simd-numerics : Math and numerics: SIMD linear algebra, geometry and intersection primitives, computational geometry, numerical robustness, mixed and double precision, deterministic math, RNG and noise, curves, quantized formats, SPMD kernels with ISA dispatch.\n94\t   - Coordinate conventions decision -> engine-architect\n95\t   - Determinism rules -> determinism-replay\n96\t== memory-allocators : Memory management: virtual memory, allocator families, thread-local and NUMA-aware allocation, tagging and attribution, budget enforcement mechanisms, fragmentation control, memory debugging, OOM policy, UMA accounting.\n97\t   - GPU heaps -> gpu-memory-resources\n98\t   - Budget numbers -> performance-architect\n99\t== containers-core-types : Containers and core types: cache-friendly containers (open-addressing maps, inline and SoA containers, rings), strings and UTF-8, interned names, hashing, bit utilities, algorithms, explicit-ownership and view types.\n100\t   - Concurrent containers -> concurrency-primitives\n101\t   - Entity handles -> entity-object-model\n102\t== concurrency-primitives : Memory model and atomics, synchronization primitives, lock-free and wait-free structures, safe memory reclamation, thread-safety annotations and model checking; reviewer for concurrent code engine-wide.\n103\t   - Scheduling -> job-system-task-graph\n104\t   - Concurrency test campaigns -> robustness-fuzzing\n105\t== job-system-task-graph : Task-parallel execution: work-stealing scheduler, dependency task graphs, fibers and C++20 coroutines, priorities and QoS, heterogeneous-core and NUMA placement, IO/GPU completion integration, parallel algorithms, blocking policy.\n106\t   - Frame phase layout -> frame-orchestration\n107\t   - IO backends -> async-io-storage\n108\t== frame-orchestration : The engine loop expressed as a task graph: frame pipelining across simulation, render and GPU, tick phases and sync points, fixed-step simulation with interpolation, time domains, latency and pacing control.\n109\t   - System ordering inside a phase -> ecs-runtime\n110\t   - Swapchain presentation -> rhi-core\n111\t== entity-object-model : Object-model strategy and identity: generational entity IDs, stable GUIDs, hard/soft/weak references, the hybrid-model policy stating which data lives in ECS vs services vs asset objects vs UI, events and messaging.\n112\t   - ECS storage and queries -> ecs-runtime\n113\t   - Asset references -> content-pipeline-architect\n114\t   - Network IDs -> replication\n115\t== ecs-runtime : ECS: storage (archetype chunks or sparse sets, chosen by ADR), queries, change detection, structural changes and command buffers, system scheduling with access-conflict analysis, relationships, singletons, authoring → runtime baking, debugging.\n116\t   - World partition -> world-architect\n117\t   - Transform propagation -> spatial-transforms\n118\t   - Object-model policy -> entity-object-model\n119\t== reflection-metadata : Type registry, reflection generation (codegen now, C++26 static reflection when toolchains allow), attributes, the property system, script-binding substrate, dynamic invocation.\n120\t   - Serialization formats -> serialization-schema\n121\t   - Editor widgets -> editor-ui-framework\n122\t   - Script VM -> scripting-runtime\n123\t== serialization-schema : Binary and text formats, schema evolution and upgraders, in-place loadable layouts, canonical deterministic serialization, portability, and validation of untrusted input.\n124\t   - Package containers -> package-formats-vfs\n125\t   - Network bit packing -> replication\n126\t   - Save-game semantics -> persistence-save\n127\t== platform-architect : Platform abstraction layer and porting strategy: OS services, CPU/GPU capability discovery, windowing, process lifecycle, capability tiers, and evaluation of new targets (web, cloud streaming).\n128\t   - Graphics API backends -> rhi-core\n129\t   - Store and online services -> platform-online-services\n130\t   - Toolchains -> build-system-toolchains\n131\t== platform-desktop : Windows, Linux, SteamOS and macOS integration: display modes, HDR and VRR capability, DPI, OS-specific IO and scheduling behavior, handheld-PC specifics, server host OS.\n132\t   - HDR signal encoding -> post-color-hdr\n133\t   - Swapchain -> rhi-core\n134\t== platform-console : Console-class integration from platform-holder documentation: OS and memory model (UMA), suspend/resume, multi-user model, devkit workflows, platform requirements feeding certification.\n135\t   - Certification tracking -> certification-compliance\n136\t   - Console graphics API backend -> rhi-core\n137\t== platform-mobile-portable : iOS, Android and portable-console integration: app lifecycle, thermal and power adaptivity, tile-based GPU implications, storage and download-size constraints.\n138\t   - Render-graph TBDR optimizations -> render-graph-scheduling\n139\t   - Touch input -> input-devices-haptics\n140\t== platform-online-services : Abstraction over first-party platform services and third-party online backends: identity and sign-in, achievements and presence, entitlements and store, cloud saves, matchmaking/lobby/session boundaries, remote config, moderation boundaries, media capture, crossplay identity.\n141\t   - Game-server hosting -> dedicated-server\n142\t   - Save-game content -> persistence-save\n143\t   - Backend implementation (outside engine scope) -> engine-architect\n144\t== input-system : Action-level input: mapping and context stacks, rebinding, buffering and latency accounting, local-multiplayer assignment, accessibility input options, UI navigation routing, per-device glyphs, recording and replay.\n145\t   - Device drivers and haptics -> input-devices-haptics\n146\t   - UI focus logic -> ui-architect\n147\t== input-devices-haptics : Device layer: keyboard/mouse raw input, gamepads, touch and gestures, motion sensors, pen, hotplug and user pairing, haptics (rumble, HD haptics, adaptive triggers).\n148\t   - Action mapping -> input-system\n149\t   - XR controllers -> xr-runtime\n150\t== xr-runtime : XR integration: OpenXR, stereo/multiview rendering hooks, foveation, reprojection and latency, XR input and hand tracking, comfort and safety requirements.\n151\t   - Render pipeline -> render-architect\n152\t   - Generic input actions -> input-system\n153\t== content-pipeline-architect : Asset identity and the content pipeline: asset registry and dependency graph, deterministic incremental per-platform cooking, the cook-step contract, derived-data cache and content-addressed store, distributed cooking, content validation.\n154\t   - Format-specific builders (shaders, animation, clusters…) -> shader-system\n155\t   - Runtime loading -> resource-streaming-architect\n156\t   - Import formats -> asset-import-interchange\n157\t== asset-import-interchange : Importers and interchange: glTF, FBX, OpenUSD, texture and audio source formats, MaterialX/OpenPBR, DCC live link, reimport and source tracking, scan data.\n158\t   - Cooking -> content-pipeline-architect\n159\t   - Material model -> material-system\n160\t== asset-cook-processors : Generic processors: texture processing and GPU texture-compression encoding, mesh optimization, hosting of collision and other domain builders under the cook contract.\n161\t   - Cluster DAG building -> virtualized-geometry-lod\n162\t   - Animation compression -> animation-runtime\n163\t   - Shader compilation -> shader-system\n164\t== resource-streaming-architect : Runtime resource model: handles and explicit lifetime, load requests with priority and deadline, dependency-aware loading, the streaming manager (budgets, eviction, prediction), fallbacks, no-stall loading.\n165\t   - IO backends -> async-io-storage\n166\t   - Package format -> package-formats-vfs\n167\t   - Texture-specific streaming -> texture-streaming-vt\n168\t== async-io-storage : Async IO: io_uring, IOCP, DirectStorage and console backends, IO scheduling and queue depth, GPU decompression, memory-mapped IO, file-system abstraction, error handling.\n169\t   - Streaming decisions -> resource-streaming-architect\n170\t   - Codec choice -> package-formats-vfs\n171\t== package-formats-vfs : Package/container format and chunking, codec selection, VFS mount layering (base, patch, DLC, mods), encryption and signing, install-chunk layout.\n172\t   - Patch generation -> packaging-release-patching\n173\t   - Relocatable data layout -> serialization-schema\n174\t== world-architect : World representation strategy (data-oriented, no universal scene graph), partitioning and streaming cells, streaming sources, HLOD strategy, simulation LOD and significance, large-world coordinate policy, level transitions, server-side world streaming.\n175\t   - World document format -> world-data-model\n176\t   - Transform math -> spatial-transforms\n177\t   - HLOD mesh generation -> virtualized-geometry-lod\n178\t== world-data-model : World and level documents, prefabs with nested overrides and variants, data layers, one-file-per-object layout for collaboration, level instances.\n179\t   - Serialization mechanics -> serialization-schema\n180\t   - Source-control workflows -> collaboration-version-control\n181\t== spatial-transforms : Transform representation and parallel hierarchy propagation, attachments, large-world coordinates implementation, generic spatial index and query service for non-physics consumers, spatial hashing.\n182\t   - Physics broadphase -> collision-detection\n183\t   - GPU culling -> gpu-driven-pipeline\n184\t== terrain : Terrain end-to-end: representation, rendering, material layering, sculpt/paint tool logic, runtime deformation, collision data hand-off.\n185\t   - Virtual texturing core -> texture-streaming-vt\n186\t   - Viewport hosting -> world-editor-viewport\n187\t   - Collision algorithms -> collision-detection\n188\t== vegetation-foliage : Vegetation instancing and rendering, procedural placement rules, wind and interaction, vegetation-specific LOD.\n189\t   - Generic PCG framework -> procedural-generation\n190\t   - Impostor generation -> virtualized-geometry-lod\n191\t== water-ocean : Ocean spectral simulation, rivers, lakes and shorelines, water surface rendering, water queries for buoyancy.\n192\t   - Buoyancy dynamics -> character-vehicle-physics\n193\t   - Fluid solvers -> fluid-simulation\n194\t== atmosphere-weather : Sky and atmospheric scattering, volumetric clouds, volumetric fog and local media, weather state and surface response, time of day.\n195\t   - Sky lighting capture for GI -> global-illumination\n196\t   - Translucency compositing -> translucency-decals\n197\t== procedural-generation : Deterministic graph-based PCG framework usable in editor and at stream-in, placement and scattering rules, grammar and constraint methods; evaluates ML generation.\n198\t   - Foliage-specific rules -> vegetation-foliage\n199\t   - Graph editor UI -> graph-editor-framework\n200\t== render-architect : Rendering architecture: pipeline organization, shading-path choice (forward+, deferred, visibility buffer), render-feature contract, render scene and world→render sync, scalability tiers from 2D mobile to path-traced, multi-view, debug modes, render threading.\n201\t   - API backends -> rhi-core\n202\t   - Pass scheduling -> render-graph-scheduling\n203\t   - Individual features (GI, shadows…) -> global-illumination\n204\t== rhi-core : Render hardware interface over D3D12, Vulkan, Metal, console APIs and WebGPU: queues and command recording, synchronization, bindless descriptors, PSOs and PSO caching, presentation, capability tiers, GPU crash breadcrumbs, driver workarounds.\n205\t   - GPU memory allocation -> gpu-memory-resources\n206\t   - Barrier planning -> render-graph-scheduling\n207\t   - Shader compilation -> shader-system\n208\t== gpu-memory-resources : GPU heaps and suballocation, residency and overcommit, upload/readback rings, sparse/reserved resources, GPU memory budgeting and defragmentation, lifetimes decoupled from frame boundaries.\n209\t   - Transient aliasing plans -> render-graph-scheduling\n210\t   - Texture streaming policy -> texture-streaming-vt\n211\t== render-graph-scheduling : Render graph declaration and compilation, automatic barriers, transient aliasing, async compute and multi-queue scheduling, TBDR pass merging, history resources, work-graph integration, general GPU compute, readback contract.\n212\t   - Heap allocation -> gpu-memory-resources\n213\t   - Feature passes -> render-architect\n214\t== shader-system : Shading language and dialect, compilation toolchain, permutations, reflection and binding layouts, interop headers, caches and distributed compilation, hot reload, shader debugging, PSO-list gathering.\n215\t   - Material graphs -> material-system\n216\t   - Runtime PSO cache -> rhi-core\n217\t== material-system : Material model (OpenPBR-class, layered), material graph → shader code generation, instances and parameters, quality tiers, material validation; evaluates neural materials.\n218\t   - BRDF research reference -> research-evidence\n219\t   - Graph editor UI -> graph-editor-framework\n220\t   - Shader compiler -> shader-system\n221\t== gpu-driven-pipeline : GPU scene and instance data, GPU frustum and two-phase occlusion culling, indirect and device-generated commands, mesh/amplification shaders, visibility-buffer rasterization, instancing, CPU-driven fallback for low-tier GPUs.\n222\t   - Cluster LOD -> virtualized-geometry-lod\n223\t   - Render-scene contract -> render-architect\n224\t== virtualized-geometry-lod : All geometric LOD: cluster hierarchies and virtualized geometry, cluster DAG building, software micro-polygon rasterization, cluster streaming, discrete LOD, HLOD proxies and impostors, deforming-geometry LOD, displacement.\n225\t   - HLOD strategy -> world-architect\n226\t   - Generic mesh optimization -> asset-cook-processors\n227\t   - RT acceleration structures -> ray-tracing-infrastructure\n228\t== texture-streaming-vt : Runtime texture formats, mip streaming, sampler-feedback streaming, virtual texturing, streaming-friendly cooked layout; evaluates neural texture compression.\n229\t   - Texture encoding in cook -> asset-cook-processors\n230\t   - Streaming manager -> resource-streaming-architect\n231\t== direct-lighting-shadows : Light types and physical units, clustered light culling, stochastic many-light sampling, area lights, cascaded, virtual and ray-traced shadows, contact shadows, light profiles.\n232\t   - Indirect lighting -> global-illumination\n233\t   - Denoisers -> reconstruction-upscaling\n234\t== global-illumination : Indirect lighting across tiers: baked lightmaps, probe volumes, screen-space GI and AO, surface/radiance-cache hybrid GI, ReSTIR GI, reflections, sky lighting, specular occlusion, SDF scene representations.\n235\t   - RT infrastructure -> ray-tracing-infrastructure\n236\t   - Atmosphere model -> atmosphere-weather\n237\t== ray-tracing-infrastructure : Acceleration structure management at scale, inline vs pipeline RT, opacity micromaps, RT LOD, software RT fallback, shader execution reordering, cluster/partitioned acceleration structures.\n238\t   - Lighting algorithms using rays -> global-illumination\n239\t   - Deformed-geometry updates -> deformation-skinning\n240\t== path-tracing : Reference path tracer as ground-truth oracle for validation, real-time path tracing, offline cinematic render mode.\n241\t   - Movie render orchestration -> cinematics-sequencer\n242\t   - Image comparison tests -> render-validation\n243\t== reconstruction-upscaling : Temporal anti-aliasing and reconstruction, temporal and ML upscalers, frame generation, dynamic resolution, the motion-vector/jitter/history contract, spatiotemporal and ML denoising, variable-rate shading.\n244\t   - Signal-specific sampling -> global-illumination\n245\t   - Frame pacing -> frame-orchestration\n246\t== post-color-hdr : Post chain, physical camera and exposure, end-to-end color management (working space, output transforms, OCIO), HDR output and calibration, tonemapping, grading.\n247\t   - Display enumeration -> platform-desktop\n248\t   - Upscaling -> reconstruction-upscaling\n249\t== translucency-decals : Transparency and OIT, refraction and distortion, decals, translucent lighting and volumetric integration.\n250\t   - Particle simulation -> vfx-particles\n251\t   - Volumetric media -> atmosphere-weather\n252\t== character-rendering : Skin subsurface scattering, eyes, strand-based hair and fur rendering, digital-human LOD.\n253\t   - Hair simulation -> cloth-deformables\n254\t   - Skinning -> deformation-skinning\n255\t== render-2d-vector : 2D draw backend shared by 2D games, UI and debug overlays: sprites, tilemaps, 2D lighting, vector paths, UI batching/clipping/SDF, HDR compositing, pixel-perfect modes.\n256\t   - Widget model -> ui-architect\n257\t   - Glyph shaping -> text-fonts\n258\t== vfx-particles : GPU particle simulation, VFX graph runtime, ribbons/beams/mesh particles, particle collision, VFX budgets and significance.\n259\t   - Physically based fluids -> fluid-simulation\n260\t   - Translucency sorting -> translucency-decals\n261\t== physics-architect : Physics architecture: build vs integrate decision, physics world representation and ECS integration, stepping and frame sync, determinism levels, physics LOD, materials, GPU offload evaluation; covers both 2D and 3D.\n262\t   - Collision algorithms -> collision-detection\n263\t   - Solvers -> rigid-body-dynamics\n264\t   - Networked physics -> prediction-rollback\n265\t== collision-detection : Shapes, broadphase, narrowphase and contact manifolds, CCD, scene queries, filtering, mesh/heightfield/SDF collision, collision cooking.\n266\t   - Generic spatial queries -> spatial-transforms\n267\t   - Dynamics -> rigid-body-dynamics\n268\t== rigid-body-dynamics : Integration and constraint solvers, joints, islands and sleeping, parallel solving, stacking stability, kinematic and animated bodies.\n269\t   - Character controllers -> character-vehicle-physics\n270\t   - Ragdoll blending -> ik-procedural-animation\n271\t== character-vehicle-physics : Character controllers (kinematic and dynamic), vehicles (wheels, tires, suspension, drivetrain), buoyancy, moving platforms and physical interaction.\n272\t   - Movement gameplay logic -> gameplay-systems-toolkit\n273\t   - Movement prediction -> prediction-rollback\n274\t== cloth-deformables : Cloth, soft bodies, ropes and cables, hair strand simulation; evaluates ML cloth.\n275\t   - Hair rendering -> character-rendering\n276\t   - Skinning -> deformation-skinning\n277\t== destruction-fracture : Fracture authoring and precomputation, runtime fracture and debris, destruction replication strategy, propagation to navigation, rendering and audio.\n278\t   - Replication mechanics -> replication\n279\t   - Navmesh rebuild -> navigation-pathfinding\n280\t== fluid-simulation : Particle fluids, grid smoke and fire, shallow-water simulation, GPU fluid solvers.\n281\t   - Ocean surface -> water-ocean\n282\t   - Artistic particles -> vfx-particles\n283\t== physics-2d : 2D rigid bodies and collision, 2D character controllers, 2D determinism.\n284\t   - 3D physics -> rigid-body-dynamics\n285\t== animation-architect : Animation architecture: data model, parallel evaluation pipeline, animation/physics/gameplay sync and root-motion policy, animation LOD, budgets.\n286\t   - Sampling and blending -> animation-runtime\n287\t   - Skinning -> deformation-skinning\n288\t== animation-runtime : Sampling and decompression, compression, blending/layering/masks/additives, retargeting, curves and notifies, 2D skeletal and flipbook animation.\n289\t   - State machines -> animation-graphs\n290\t   - IK -> ik-procedural-animation\n291\t== deformation-skinning : GPU skinning (linear, dual quaternion), morph targets, ML deformers, deformed-geometry acceleration-structure updates, deformation motion vectors.\n292\t   - Cloth -> cloth-deformables\n293\t   - Facial solvers -> facial-animation\n294\t== animation-graphs : Animation graphs and state machines, blend spaces, graph compilation and data-driven evaluation, graph debugging and rewind.\n295\t   - Graph editor UI -> graph-editor-framework\n296\t   - Motion matching -> motion-synthesis\n297\t== motion-synthesis : Motion matching, learned motion matching and neural controllers, pose databases, trajectory prediction and gameplay coupling.\n298\t   - ML runtime -> ml-inference-runtime\n299\t   - Locomotion gameplay -> gameplay-systems-toolkit\n300\t== ik-procedural-animation : IK solvers, foot placement, procedural animation, physical animation and active ragdoll.\n301\t   - Rigid-body solver -> rigid-body-dynamics\n302\t   - Motion matching -> motion-synthesis\n303\t== facial-animation : Facial rigs and solvers, audio-driven and ML lip sync, performance-capture import.\n304\t   - Face rendering -> character-rendering\n305\t   - Dialogue playback -> audio-content-runtime\n306\t== cinematics-sequencer : Timeline/sequencer, camera cuts and cinematic cameras, high-quality movie rendering, cutscene streaming and preloading.\n307\t   - Gameplay camera -> gameplay-systems-toolkit\n308\t   - Path tracer -> path-tracing\n309\t== audio-architect : Audio engine architecture and threading, device backends, voice management and virtualization, middleware decision, audio budgets.\n310\t   - DSP algorithms -> audio-dsp-mixing\n311\t   - Spatialization -> spatial-audio-acoustics\n312\t== audio-dsp-mixing : Mixer graph and buses, DSP effects and convolution reverb, dynamics and loudness, codecs and decoding, audio streaming, procedural synthesis, voice-chat capture and processing.\n313\t   - Voice-chat transport -> network-transport\n314\t   - Spatialization -> spatial-audio-acoustics\n315\t== spatial-audio-acoustics : Panning and distance, HRTF, ambisonics, object-based output, occlusion and obstruction, acoustic propagation, reverb environments.\n316\t   - Collision queries -> collision-detection\n317\t   - Mixer -> audio-dsp-mixing\n318\t== audio-content-runtime : Audio event system and parameters, interactive music, dialogue and VO, authoring tool integration, audio-to-haptics.\n319\t   - Localization pipeline -> localization-i18n\n320\t   - Haptics devices -> input-devices-haptics\n321\t== network-architect : Netcode model per game type (authoritative server, lockstep, rollback, P2P/relay), network tick and time, authority model, budgets and scale targets, protocol versioning, sharded worlds evaluation.\n322\t   - Transport -> network-transport\n323\t   - Replication mechanics -> replication\n324\t   - Matchmaking services -> platform-online-services\n325\t== network-transport : UDP sockets and platform network APIs, reliability and ordering, fragmentation, congestion control, encryption and authentication, NAT traversal and relays, connection lifecycle, link simulation, QUIC/WebTransport evaluation.\n326\t   - What is replicated -> replication\n327\t   - Relay service operation -> platform-online-services\n328\t== replication : Entity and property replication, delta compression and quantization, interest management, prioritization, RPCs, snapshot interpolation, replay recording, network ID mapping.\n329\t   - Prediction -> prediction-rollback\n330\t   - Transport -> network-transport\n331\t== prediction-rollback : Client prediction and reconciliation, rollback netcode, lag compensation, deterministic lockstep, networked physics, clock synchronization.\n332\t   - Determinism rules -> determinism-replay\n333\t   - Physics solver -> rigid-body-dynamics\n334\t== dedicated-server : Headless server builds and stripping, tick cost and multi-instance density, fleet orchestration boundary, server observability, listen servers and host migration.\n335\t   - Fleet operation (outside engine scope) -> platform-online-services\n336\t   - Server logging substrate -> observability-telemetry\n337\t== gameplay-architect : Gameplay framework: rules, players and possession, extension points and game-module structure, game flow and transitions, local players.\n338\t   - Abilities/tags/camera toolkit -> gameplay-systems-toolkit\n339\t   - Scripting VM -> scripting-runtime\n340\t   - Game-specific code (the game team) -> engine-architect\n341\t== gameplay-systems-toolkit : Reusable gameplay systems: abilities, effects and attributes, gameplay tags, camera system, spawning and pooling, gameplay message routing, photo mode.\n342\t   - Generic events -> entity-object-model\n343\t   - Cinematic cameras -> cinematics-sequencer\n344\t== scripting-runtime : Scripting language selection, VM embedding and bindings, sandboxing, debugging and profiling, hot reload, visual scripting, AOT/JIT constraints, GC policy.\n345\t   - Reflection substrate -> reflection-metadata\n346\t   - Graph editor UI -> graph-editor-framework\n347\t== navigation-pathfinding : Navmesh generation (tiled, runtime rebuild), grid and hierarchical pathfinding, path following, off-mesh links, 3D/volumetric navigation.\n348\t   - Crowd avoidance -> crowd-simulation\n349\t   - Decision making -> ai-behavior-perception\n350\t== crowd-simulation : Flow fields, crowd avoidance, mass-agent simulation and LOD.\n351\t   - Navmesh -> navigation-pathfinding\n352\t   - Individual AI decisions -> ai-behavior-perception\n353\t== ai-behavior-perception : Decision making (behavior trees, utility, HTN/GOAP, state trees), perception, environment queries, smart objects, AI scheduling and LOD; evaluates learned and LLM-driven agents.\n354\t   - Navigation -> navigation-pathfinding\n355\t   - ML runtime -> ml-inference-runtime\n356\t== persistence-save : Save-game model and serialization, save versioning and migration, atomic writes, platform save APIs and quotas, cloud-save sync, persistent world-state deltas, checkpoints.\n357\t   - Schema evolution mechanism -> serialization-schema\n358\t   - Cloud service API -> platform-online-services\n359\t== ui-architect : UI architecture (retained with data binding for game UI, immediate for developer UI), layout, styling, focus and navigation, animation, in-world UI, designer tool logic, UI performance.\n360\t   - UI draw backend -> render-2d-vector\n361\t   - Text shaping -> text-fonts\n362\t   - Editor panels -> editor-ui-framework\n363\t== text-fonts : Font loading and fallback, glyph rasterization, shaping, bidi and line breaking, rich text and emoji, text input and IME.\n364\t   - String content -> localization-i18n\n365\t   - 2D draw submission -> render-2d-vector\n366\t== localization-i18n : String tables, ICU-class message formatting, CLDR locale formatting, localization pipeline, pseudo-localization, localized asset variants, culturalization.\n367\t   - Glyph rendering -> text-fonts\n368\t   - VO playback -> audio-content-runtime\n369\t== editor-architect : Editor architecture: process model (in- vs out-of-process runtime), editor/runtime data separation, transactions and undo/redo, selection, extension API and tool scripting, play-in-editor isolation, remote live editing, headless editor, large-project performance.\n370\t   - Panels and inspectors -> editor-ui-framework\n371\t   - World viewport tools -> world-editor-viewport\n372\t   - Source control -> collaboration-version-control\n373\t== editor-ui-framework : Tool UI toolkit (docking, panels), reflection-driven inspectors, asset browser, immediate-mode developer UI, editor UX standards.\n374\t   - Game UI -> ui-architect\n375\t   - Graph editors -> graph-editor-framework\n376\t== world-editor-viewport : Viewport and navigation, gizmos, snapping and placement, partition-aware world editing, spline tools, environment tool-mode hosting.\n377\t   - Terrain tool logic -> terrain\n378\t   - World format -> world-data-model\n379\t== graph-editor-framework : Shared node-graph editor for material, animation, VFX, audio, PCG and visual-script graphs: framework, compile/validation contract, debugging, diff and merge.\n380\t   - Each domain's graph semantics -> material-system\n381\t== collaboration-version-control : Source-control integration, locking and checkout, multi-user concurrent editing, merge tooling for scene and asset data, content review, large-binary storage strategy.\n382\t   - Branching model -> build-release-architect\n383\t   - File-per-object layout -> world-data-model\n384\t== visual-debugging-tools : Debug draw API, in-game console and cheats, runtime entity inspector and gameplay debugger, visual logger and rewind, debug menus and overlays.\n385\t   - Logging and traces -> observability-telemetry\n386\t   - Render buffer visualization -> render-architect\n387\t== ai-assisted-authoring : Evaluates and integrates AI-assisted authoring: generative asset tools, editor copilots, ML-assisted retopology/rigging/UV/LOD, provenance and licensing of generated content.\n388\t   - Runtime inference -> ml-inference-runtime\n389\t   - License compliance sign-off -> certification-compliance\n390\t== build-release-architect : Build and release architecture: branching and merge model, engine release management and versioning, orchestration of the code → content → package pipeline.\n391\t   - Build system implementation -> build-system-toolchains\n392\t   - CI pipelines -> ci-cd-automation\n393\t   - Packaging -> packaging-release-patching\n394\t== build-system-toolchains : Build graph, compiler and toolchain matrix, C++ modules/unity/PCH, compile caching and distribution, codegen integration, third-party dependencies, static analysis, build configurations.\n395\t   - CI orchestration -> ci-cd-automation\n396\t   - Supply-chain policy -> security-engineering\n397\t== ci-cd-automation : CI pipelines, build farm and artifact storage, pre-submit and merge gating, symbol servers, device-farm orchestration, developer CLI and automation.\n398\t   - What tests exist -> test-architect\n399\t   - Perf thresholds -> performance-architect\n400\t== packaging-release-patching : Platform packaging and signing, store-submission artifacts, delta/chunk patching, DLC, install-on-demand, client/server/content version compatibility, CDN boundary, release rollback.\n401\t   - Package runtime format -> package-formats-vfs\n402\t   - Certification tracking -> certification-compliance\n403\t"}]},"uuid":"b033b0b5-f9a5-44cf-bec3-06412cc0f877","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:45:34.487Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"da6d22fa-95f5-4d97-88dc-17a927c6200f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
